[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3825387293","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115649#issuecomment-3825387293","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115649","id":3825387293,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7kAscd","user":{"login":"ashtonmeuser","id":7253863,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNTM4NjM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7253863?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser","html_url":"https://github.com/ashtonmeuser","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-30T19:35:04Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T19:35:04Z","body":"This doesn't address syntax highlighting, etc. which is, in my opinion, a separate issue. Note that other constants like `OP_MAX` do not appear highlighted.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3825387293/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3825494719","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115649#issuecomment-3825494719","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115649","id":3825494719,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7kBGq_","user":{"login":"geekley","id":38332912,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4MzMyOTEy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38332912?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley","html_url":"https://github.com/geekley","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-30T20:02:37Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T20:15:12Z","body":"Isn't uint64 max gonna overflow in GDScript, since the `int` type is 64-bit signed?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3825494719/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3825529941","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115649#issuecomment-3825529941","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115649","id":3825529941,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7kBPRV","user":{"login":"geekley","id":38332912,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4MzMyOTEy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38332912?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley","html_url":"https://github.com/geekley","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-30T20:11:45Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T20:25:03Z","body":"Also, I'd suggest using the name conventions in my comment, where I define reasoning and even add float constants too with completely unambiguous precise names (check my gist)\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/2411#issuecomment-2014279878\r\nhttps://gist.github.com/geekley/5bf72d3cbaa1da196545bee977ee8eda\r\n\r\nI suggested using NEGATIVE_LIMIT instead of MIN for the negative integers for several reasons:\r\n- MIN can imply a \"close to zero\" meaning (if we think about the same convention being used for floats)\r\n  so \"max negative\" would be clearer\r\n- However \"max negative\" could confuse someone thinking it's the negative of \"max positive\", so NEGATIVE_LIMIT is clearer about the asymmetry. That asymmetry is important because this value is special: it overflows to itself when negated, so it has no negative that can be represented (similar to zero not having one either). It may be often used to represent \"invalid\" values for this reason. I think it's a good idea to have a name that represents this asymmetry, specially for beginners who may not be familiar with how 2's complement works.\r\n- Use just MAX instead of \"max positive\" so one can do `-INTx_MAX` for its negative\r\n  (as \"minus max positive\" would be a bit weird)\r\n\r\nAlso I'm using precise names for float constants instead of something vague like \"epsilon\".","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3825529941/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3825611445","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115649#issuecomment-3825611445","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115649","id":3825611445,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7kBjK1","user":{"login":"ashtonmeuser","id":7253863,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNTM4NjM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7253863?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser","html_url":"https://github.com/ashtonmeuser","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-30T20:31:38Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T20:31:38Z","body":"> Isn't uint64 max gonna overflow in GDScript, since the int type is 64-bit signed?\r\n\r\nGreat point, @geekley. Suggestions?\r\n\r\n> MIN can imply a \"close to zero\" meaning (if we think about the same convention being used for floats)\r\nso \"max negative\" would be clearer\r\n\r\nI see your reasoning, but I'd argue that it's obvious enough to anyone reaching for these constants that it's the mathematical definition of minimum. It's also obvious that if you want to use `min(abs(a), abs(b))` that you'd just use zero (0). Your same point could be used against the `min()` function itself.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3825611445/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3825646586","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115649#issuecomment-3825646586","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115649","id":3825646586,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7kBrv6","user":{"login":"geekley","id":38332912,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4MzMyOTEy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38332912?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley","html_url":"https://github.com/geekley","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-30T20:40:52Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T20:40:52Z","body":"About uint64_max, I guess for GDScript nothing can be done, it's just not supported.\r\nAdding it as a float or string value doesn't make sense. Since it's not supported, probably people won't need to use this constant. So just remove it.\r\n\r\nIf you really want to, you could add the number itself in the docs of uint32_max and int64_max as an additional note saying \"that value would be the max for UINT_64, but it cannot be represented in GDScript because the `int` type can only hold up to 64-bit signed values\".","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3825646586/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3825657409","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115649#issuecomment-3825657409","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115649","id":3825657409,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7kBuZB","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-30T20:44:22Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T20:44:22Z","body":"> > Isn't uint64 max gonna overflow in GDScript, since the int type is 64-bit signed?\r\n> \r\n> Great point, geekley. Suggestions?\r\n\r\nI would suggest removing `UINT64_MAX`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3825657409/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3825669788","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115649#issuecomment-3825669788","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115649","id":3825669788,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7kBxac","user":{"login":"geekley","id":38332912,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4MzMyOTEy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38332912?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley","html_url":"https://github.com/geekley","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-30T20:48:19Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T20:55:19Z","body":"> the mathematical definition of minimum\r\n\r\nWell like I said above, I'd argue that value is special because it being a 2's complement limit makes it so it doesn't follow the mathematical definitions of numbers -- it's non-zero, but if negated, it will overflow to itself.\r\nSo I think it makes sense to use a distinct name to make explicit that kind of asymmetry -- as I believe most of the time someone uses that value, the purpose will likely be more about limits or a special value (e.g. \"invalid\") rather than for doing normal numerical calculations or comparisons.\r\n\r\nSo I think \"negative limit\" is a distinctive name from \"max/min\" yet clearly conveys the intended meaning. I think that would be more friendly to beginners (my understanding is that GDScript is a language aimed to beginners in programming, but feel free to correct me if I'm wrong).\r\n\r\nAnother option would be \"INT*_MAX\" and \"INT*_LIMIT_MIN\"; my point is more so to make the names asymmetrical so you don't forget that one value is not the negation of the other.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3825669788/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":0,"-1":3,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3825670172","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115649#issuecomment-3825670172","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115649","id":3825670172,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7kBxgc","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-30T20:48:24Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T20:48:51Z","body":"Note that we have String's `num_uint64`, which means we do have limited capacity for treating `int` as `uint64_t` instead of the usual `int64_t`. \r\nHowever, I would agree to omit `UINT64_MAX` anyway. If we add it it's guaranteed to lead to confusion.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3825670172/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3825723568","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115649#issuecomment-3825723568","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115649","id":3825723568,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7kB-iw","user":{"login":"geekley","id":38332912,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4MzMyOTEy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38332912?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley","html_url":"https://github.com/geekley","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-30T21:04:37Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T21:04:37Z","body":"I also didn't see any discussion about whether these constants should be global or added under `int` and `float`, e.g. `int.INT8_MAX`. Either is fine to me, but one could argue people may expect them under the types, consistent with cases like `Vector3i.MAX`.\r\n\r\nUnless it's not even doable lol.\r\nCan `int` and `float` not even have constants or static members? Impossible? Design choice?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3825723568/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3825887863","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115649#issuecomment-3825887863","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115649","id":3825887863,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7kCmp3","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-30T21:38:40Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T21:38:40Z","body":"> I also didn't see any discussion about whether these constants should be global or added under `int` and `float`, e.g. `int.INT8_MAX`. Either is fine to me, but one could argue people may expect them under the types, consistent with cases like `Vector3i.MAX`.\r\n\r\nIf we only wanted to add `INT64_MIN` and `INT64_MAX`, it would make sense to add them as `int.MIN` and `int.MAX`. But the other constants don't directly relate to `int`. And we don't have types like `int8` and `uint32`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3825887863/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3825928202","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115649#issuecomment-3825928202","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115649","id":3825928202,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7kCwgK","user":{"login":"geekley","id":38332912,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4MzMyOTEy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38332912?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley","html_url":"https://github.com/geekley","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-30T21:48:34Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T21:50:53Z","body":"> If we only wanted to add `INT64_MIN` and `INT64_MAX`, it would make sense to add them as `int.MIN` and `int.MAX`. But the other constants don't directly relate to `int`. And we don't have types like `int8` and `uint32`.\r\n\r\n@dalexeev Would it make sense to add all bits globally and also duplicate the 64-bit ones as `int.MAX` etc? (and eventually `float.MAX_*` etc) So people can easily get `int` max without having to care/remember it's 64-bit? GDScript does have some duplicate definitions e.g. `append|push_back`, `s.length()|len(s)` etc.\r\n\r\nOr is it a design intention to keep lowercase `bool|int|float` types empty of any members except operators?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3825928202/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3827525169","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115649#issuecomment-3827525169","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115649","id":3827525169,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7kI2Yx","user":{"login":"ashtonmeuser","id":7253863,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNTM4NjM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7253863?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser","html_url":"https://github.com/ashtonmeuser","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-31T05:13:47Z","updated_at":"2026-01-31T05:13:47Z","body":"Didn't expect it to go this deep, but this is actually reliant on https://github.com/godotengine/godot-cpp/pull/1916. The global constants are exposed by `extension_api.json` and ingested by godot-cpp which spits them out as constants in _godot-cpp/gen/include/godot_cpp/classes/global_constants.hpp_. These constants conflict with macros from `cstdint`. Therefore, we'll simply ignore them in godot-cpp as their values are already available via a standard lib.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3827525169/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3827544791","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115649#issuecomment-3827544791","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115649","id":3827544791,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7kI7LX","user":{"login":"ashtonmeuser","id":7253863,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNTM4NjM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7253863?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser","html_url":"https://github.com/ashtonmeuser","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-31T05:24:29Z","updated_at":"2026-01-31T05:24:29Z","body":"> Would it make sense to add all bits globally and also duplicate the 64-bit ones as int.MAX etc?\r\n\r\nI'm lukewarm on this but adding min/max constants to the types themselves could be an entirely separate PR.\r\n\r\nSimply exposing these constants to GDScript in _any_ fashion has been talked about for ages with little traction, so I'd vote that we merge a minimal implementation and save the architectural/enhancement conversation for https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals. Particularly so if the `int.MAX` suggestion is in addition to the implementation found in this PR.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3827544791/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3827596025","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115649#issuecomment-3827596025","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115649","id":3827596025,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7kJHr5","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-31T05:54:49Z","updated_at":"2026-01-31T05:54:49Z","body":"> Or is it a design intention to keep lowercase `bool|int|float` types empty of any members except operators?\r\n\r\nI wouldn't say this is a hard limitation or a deliberate design decision, but in many Godot language bindings, the primitive types (`bool`, `int`, and `float`) are translated into the corresponding built-in primitive types, which can't always be modified. So, we could absolutely have `int.MIN` and `int.MAX` in GDScript, but in other languages, this might be impossible or pointless (because the language already has its own limit constants).\r\n\r\nShould we add limit constants for GDScript that most language bindings will ignore? I don't have a strong opinion on this. On the one hand, it makes sense. On the other hand, GDScript only has one integer type, and there's relatively little need for this feature to justify adding aliases.\r\n\r\nAnother question is whether these constants should be in `@GlobalScope` or `@GDScript`, given that many languages ​​have their own constants (as well as functions like `min()`, `sin()`, and so on, which are nevertheless located in `@GlobalScope`). The advantage of addition the limit constants to `@GDScript` is that we won't need to modify the binding generator in `godot-cpp`. The disadvantage is complexity (constants like `PI` and `NAN` are implemented as literals in GDScript, not resolved by the analyzer) and unclear criteria for when something should go into `@GlobalScope` and when into `@GDScript`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3827596025/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3917778790","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115649#issuecomment-3917778790","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115649","id":3917778790,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7phI9m","user":{"login":"ashtonmeuser","id":7253863,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNTM4NjM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7253863?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser","html_url":"https://github.com/ashtonmeuser","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashtonmeuser/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-18T00:24:55Z","updated_at":"2026-02-18T00:24:55Z","body":"Note that GHA will continue to fail until https://github.com/godotengine/godot-cpp/pull/1916 is merged and cherry picked to the godot-cpp branch used by Godot (4.5). See conversation on that PR.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3917778790/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3919895253","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115649#issuecomment-3919895253","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115649","id":3919895253,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ppNrV","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-18T10:10:16Z","updated_at":"2026-02-18T10:10:52Z","body":"> Another question is whether these constants should be in @GlobalScope or @GDScript, given that many languages ​​have their own constants (as well as functions like min(), sin(), and so on, which are nevertheless located in @GlobalScope). The advantage of addition the limit constants to @GDScript is that we won't need to modify the binding generator in godot-cpp. The disadvantage is complexity (constants like PI and NAN are implemented as literals in GDScript, not resolved by the analyzer) and unclear criteria for when something should go into @GlobalScope and when into @GDScript.\r\n\r\nI agree with Akien's concern (from RC) that exposing these constants to other languages is not needed, especially given how it was already causing problems for godot-cpp. I'd say these should be GDScript-only.\r\n\r\nMy naive recommendation (given my lack of GDScript code knowledge) for how this should be approached is to inject these values as constants, i.e. at the same level where it would have ended up if it was exposed via `@GlobalScope`. That's how i did it for an experimental programming language anyway, and it worked out pretty well architecturally.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3919895253/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3920029713","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115649#issuecomment-3920029713","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115649","id":3920029713,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ppugR","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-18T10:35:49Z","updated_at":"2026-02-18T10:35:49Z","body":"We could add these constants to `@GDScript` (as it is implemented for `PI`, `TAU`, `INF`, and `NAN`), but that would require more boilerplate (these constants are implemented as keywords/literals in the tokenizer). Alternatively, we could fix this system by resolving the constants through the analyzer.\r\n\r\nBut I'm not sure this is conceptually correct. Most other languages ​​have their own mathematical functions like `min()` and `sin()`, but we still have them in `@GlobalScope`, not `@GDScript`. In my opinion, filtering out numeric limit constants in binding generators if the target language already has the corresponding constants is a good approach.\r\n\r\nIn my opinion, we should move `PI`, `TAU`, `INF`, `NAN` from `@GDScript` to `@GlobalScope`, since the core documentation refers to these constants, and this can cause problems if the `gdscript` module is disabled.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"420\" height=\"402\" alt=\"\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c4c61edf-5f2e-4548-adb8-cb374a5e9ca7\" />","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3920029713/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3920919548","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115649#issuecomment-3920919548","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115649","id":3920919548,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ptHv8","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-18T13:45:25Z","updated_at":"2026-02-18T13:45:25Z","body":"Agreed on moving `PI`, `TAU`, `INF`, `NAN` from `@GDScript` to `@GlobalScope`, but that should be its own PR","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3920919548/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3936252382","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115649#issuecomment-3936252382","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115649","id":3936252382,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7qnnHe","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-20T17:41:38Z","updated_at":"2026-02-20T17:41:38Z","body":"Thanks! Congratulations on your first merged contribution! 🎉 ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3936252382/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":3,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]